    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 6 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Achieve the lowest total score at the end of nine 'holes' (rounds).",
      'Turn-flow example: 1. Players take turns clockwise.\n2. ACTION: Draw the top card from the stock OR the top card from the discard pile.\n3. REPLACEMENT: Use the drawn card to replace any one of your six cards (face-up or face-down). The replaced card is discarded face-up.\n4. DISCARDING: If drawing from the stock, you may choose to discard the card immediately instead of using it to replace, but you must then turn one of your face-down cards face-up.\n5. ENDING: When a player has all cards face-up, everyone else gets one final turn. Then scores are tallied.',
      "Scoring example: Players tally their card values at the end of each round. Rounds continue for nine 'holes'. Lowest total score after 9 rounds wins..",
